## ⚠️ Important Notice — PyMuPDF / MuPDF (GNU AGPL v3)

This project depends on **PyMuPDF** (`fitz`), which is licensed under the
**GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0)** by Artifex Software, Inc.

The AGPL is a strong copyleft license. Its key requirement:

> If you run a modified version of an AGPL-licensed program on a server and allow
> users to interact with it over a network, you must make the **complete source code**
> of your modified version available to those users.

**What this means in practice:**

| Use case | What you must do |
|---|---|
| Personal / local use | Nothing extra required |
| Private internal deployment | Nothing extra required |
| Public open-source project | Keep your project open-source and AGPL-compatible |
| Public web service / SaaS | Publish your full source code (this repo already does that) |
| Commercial / closed-source product | Obtain a commercial license from Artifex — see [artifex.com/licensing](https://artifex.com/licensing) |

**This repository is publicly available on GitHub, which satisfies the AGPL source-disclosure requirement for the author's own deployment.**

The MIT license grant above applies only to the original code in this repository. It does not override or supersede the AGPL obligations introduced by PyMuPDF. If you are unsure about your specific situation, consult a qualified legal professional.

