This project installs the following open-source libraries. Each is governed by its own license. They are listed here for transparency and compliance.

| Library | License | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Flask | BSD-3-Clause | Web framework |
| Werkzeug | BSD-3-Clause | WSGI utilities |
| python-dotenv | BSD-3-Clause | Environment variable loading |
| PyMuPDF (fitz) | **GNU AGPL v3.0** | ⚠️ See notice above |
| pypdf | BSD-3-Clause | Pure-Python PDF reading/writing |
| ReportLab | BSD | PDF generation |
| pdf2docx | MIT | PDF → Word conversion |
| docx2pdf | MIT | Word → PDF conversion |
| python-docx | MIT | Word document manipulation |
| python-pptx | MIT | PowerPoint manipulation |
| pdfplumber | MIT | PDF text/table extraction |
| Pillow | HPND (MIT-style) | Image processing |
| NumPy | BSD-3-Clause | Numerical computing |
| rembg | MIT | AI background removal |
| opencv-python | Apache 2.0 | Computer vision |
| pytesseract | Apache 2.0 | Python wrapper for Tesseract OCR |
| Tesseract OCR | Apache 2.0 | OCR engine (external binary) |
| requests | Apache 2.0 | HTTP client |
| openpyxl | MIT | Excel file reading/writing |
| pandas | BSD-3-Clause | Data manipulation |
| Markdown | BSD-3-Clause | Markdown parsing |
| qrcode | MIT | QR code generation |
| sumy | MIT | Offline text summarization |
| nltk | Apache 2.0 | Natural language processing |
| deep-translator | MIT | Translation via Google Translate |
| spacy | MIT | NLP / keyword extraction |
| weasyprint | BSD-3-Clause | HTML/CSS → PDF rendering |
| breadability | Apache 2.0 | Article text extraction |

None of these libraries are modified by this project. They are used as-is via standard package installation (`pip install`). Their licenses are not affected by this project's MIT license.

